void addRoundKey_hls(unsigned char block[PRESENT_BLOCK_SIZE_BYTES], 
                    unsigned char roundKey[ROUND_KEY_SIZE_BYTES]) 
{
    #pragma HLS ARRAY_PARTITION variable=block complete dim=1
    #pragma HLS ARRAY_PARTITION variable=roundKey complete dim=1
    
    for (int i = 0; i < PRESENT_BLOCK_SIZE_BYTES; i++) {
        #pragma HLS UNROLL yes
        block[i] ^= roundKey[i];
    }
}

void addRoundKey(block_t *block, round_key_t *roundKey) {
    addRoundKey_hls(*block, *roundKey);
}
```

This enhanced optimization:
1. Adds array partitioning pragmas to decompose arrays into individual registers
2. Maintains full loop unrolling for maximum parallelism
3. Enables true parallel XOR operations by eliminating memory access bottlenecks
4. Reduces latency to theoretical minimum (1 cycle operation)
5. Increases register usage but should dramatically improve timing

The array partitioning pragmas help HLS tools understand that all elements can be accessed simultaneously, while the unroll pragma ensures spatial parallelism of the XOR operations. This combination attacks both the computation and memory access aspects of the latency problem.
